INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('gear_axepick_rift', 'gear', 'icon', 'Sprites/Icons/Gear/gear_axepick_rift', 64, 64, 1, 16, 'Point', 'purple', 'Dark fantasy RPG item icon, flat illustration, transparent background, readable at 64px, ink linework, centered composition, high silhouette clarity. Epic tier (purple glow). Subject: Void-cracked pick — a miner’s pickaxe weapon with a jagged rift fracture running through the metal spike. The spike tip is “phase-touched”: show rift energy concentrated at the very tip, implying it can pass through armor on heavy strikes.

Key design details:

- Pick head: one dominant spike (the “phasing” spike) with a visible void crack along its length; opposite side can be a blunt hammer face or a smaller counter-spike (keep secondary)
- Rift damage: fractured metal edges, with the crack acting like a thin tear (abstract void geometry, no runes/text)
- Haft: dark wood handle with a simple leather wrap near the grip; 1–2 iron bands (minimal)

Epic purple glow / VFX treatment:

- Concentrate the brightest violet energy at the spike tip (small, intense highlight cluster)
- Add a tight rim-glow along the crack and a few short “phase wisps” peeling off the tip (thin, controlled strokes; no big bloom)
- Use 2–3 stepped glow bands max: deep indigo outer → violet core → pale lavender highlight (kept close to silhouette)

Style constraints:

- Bold ink linework + sparse crosshatching only (stay readable at 64px)
- Limited flat shading (2–3 values), avoid painterly texture
- Transparent background, no frame unless your icon set uses one
- No text, no watermark, no logos')
