- Monocle frame: tarnished metal ring (dark iron/blackened brass), simple but ominous; small chain link nub or clasp hint (optional, minimal)
- Lens: one dominant jagged fracture line across the glass (clean, readable crack pattern, not spiderweb noise)
- Void eye: an abstract eye shape behind/within the crack (dark void iris/pupil), with a thin jade rim-light outlining the eye where it intersects the crack
- Corruption accents: a few ledger-like “tally” ticks or geometric accounting marks etched on the rim (abstract shapes only, not readable text)

Palette / lighting:

- Primary accent: jade green #32C882 (use for rim-glow and small energy highlights)
- Void base: near-black / deep purple-black shadows
- Glow: tight, controlled jade rim-glow hugging the monocle edge and crack line (pixel-stepped bands if needed; no big soft bloom)
- Keep highlights sparse so the jade reads as “corruption energy” rather than neon

Style constraints:

- Bold ink linework with minimal crosshatching (stays readable at 64px)
- Limited flat shading (2–3 values max), avoid painterly texture
- No background elements, no frame unless your icon set uses one
- No readable text, no watermark')
