INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('vfx_ability_vine_snare', 'vfx', 'vfx', 'Sprites/VFX/vfx_ability_vine_snare', 320, 96, 5, 32, 'Point', '#32C882', 'Pixel art VFX sprite sheet, 5-frame horizontal strip, 320x96 total, exactly 5 frames in ONE ROW left-to-right, each frame 64x96. Dark background #0C0C14. CRITICAL LAYOUT: uniform 64x96 cells, no extra frames, no gaps, no scattered placement. Hard pixel edges, no anti-aliasing, no blur, zero alpha bleed.

Effect: Vine eruption — jade-green thorned vines bursting from soil (snare/root effect). Center the origin point near the bottom third of the frame; vines grow upward and outward, readable silhouettes with chunky pixel clusters (avoid noisy tangles).

Frame beats (left→right):

1) Frame 1 (Ground crack): jagged crack in soil at center-bottom with a faint jade glow inside the裂 (1–2 px band only). A couple tiny thorn tips barely visible.

2) Frame 2 (First shoot): one main vine shoot bursts up (strong S-curve), plus 1 small secondary shoot. Add 2–4 visible thorns (simple triangular pixels) along the main shoot.

3) Frame 3 (Spread): 2–3 vines now, branching outward left/right; introduce a few leaf-like hooks or barbs pointing inward (snare feel). Growth reaches mid-height.

4) Frame 4 (Entangle): vines widen into a snare pattern—more wrapping arcs, thicker base at ground, a few thorn clusters near the midsection. Keep negative space so the shape reads.

5) Frame 5 (Full snare bloom): maximum spread: a “cage” of thorned vines with a clear center pocket where a unit would be trapped. Add a subtle jade highlight band on outer edges (pixel-stepped), but keep the interior mostly dark for readability.

Palette/lighting:

- Core vine: deep green + jade green
- Highlights: bright jade/acid-green on a few edge pixels only
- Optional shadow: near-black/very dark green for depth
- No smooth gradients; any glow must be pixel-stepped and tight (1–2 px max)

Negative prompts: no flowers, no realistic ivy texture, no brown tree trunks, no smooth glow bloom, no dirt splash particles, no text, no watermark, no background scenery beyond the crack cue.')
ON CONFLICT (asset_key) DO UPDATE SET
  category = EXCLUDED.category, tier = EXCLUDED.tier, unity_path = EXCLUDED.unity_path,
  target_w = EXCLUDED.target_w, target_h = EXCLUDED.target_h, frame_count = EXCLUDED.frame_count,
  ppu = EXCLUDED.ppu, filter_mode = EXCLUDED.filter_mode,
  primary_color = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.primary_color, public.sprite_assets.primary_color),
  prompt_template = EXCLUDED.prompt_template;

INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('vfx_ability_void_burst', 'vfx', 'vfx', 'Sprites/VFX/vfx_ability_void_burst', 384, 96, 6, 32, 'Point', '#7C4DFF', 'Pixel art VFX sprite sheet, 6-frame horizontal strip, 384x96 total, exactly 6 frames in ONE ROW left-to-right, each frame 64x96. Dark background #0C0C14. CRITICAL LAYOUT: uniform 64x96 cells, no extra frames, no gaps, no scattered placement. Hard pixel edges, no anti-aliasing, no blur, zero alpha bleed.

Effect: Void Burst explosion — electric violet eruption from ground up (centered on a ground contact point near the bottom third of the frame). High readability, chunky pixel clusters, minimal noise.

Frame beats (left→right):

1) Frame 1 (Seed crack): thin void crack in the ground at center-bottom (jagged 1px line with a few 2px splits). Tiny violet core glow inside the crack only (1–2 px band).

2) Frame 2 (Column rise): a tight energy column shoots upward from the crack (narrow at base, slightly widening). Brightest core in the centerline; small pixel sparks eject upward.

3) Frame 3 (Burst start): column blossoms into an expanding radial burst—starburst spikes and a circular shock ring begin forming. Keep spikes chunky and symmetric-ish.

4) Frame 4 (Peak): largest radial burst (maximum radius), strongest electric-violet intensity. Add a few arcing “lightning” pixel zigzags around the outer edge (simple 1px/2px steps, not scribbly).

5) Frame 5 (Afterglow ring): explosion collapses to a clean expanding ring + faint vertical residue. Ring is thinner, more defined; interior mostly empty/dim.

6) Frame 6 (Fade): near-empty; only a faint broken ring remnant and 2–4 tiny violet motes drifting upward (or fully empty if you want a hard end).

Palette/lighting:

- Core: electric violet + magenta-violet + pale lavender highlights (limited)
- Shadows: deep indigo/near-black for contrast against #0C0C14
- Glow must be pixel-stepped (2–3 bands), no smooth gradients, no bloom

Negative prompts: no smoke, no fog, no orange/yellow fire, no smooth radial gradients, no text, no watermark, no background scenery beyond the ground crack cue.')
ON CONFLICT (asset_key) DO UPDATE SET
  category = EXCLUDED.category, tier = EXCLUDED.tier, unity_path = EXCLUDED.unity_path,
  target_w = EXCLUDED.target_w, target_h = EXCLUDED.target_h, frame_count = EXCLUDED.frame_count,
  ppu = EXCLUDED.ppu, filter_mode = EXCLUDED.filter_mode,
  primary_color = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.primary_color, public.sprite_assets.primary_color),
  prompt_template = EXCLUDED.prompt_template;

INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('vfx_death_enemy', 'vfx', 'vfx', 'Sprites/VFX/vfx_death_enemy', 320, 64, 5, 32, 'Point', '#CC2020', 'Pixel art VFX sprite sheet, 5-frame horizontal strip, 320x64 total, exactly 5 frames in ONE ROW left-to-right, each frame 64x64. Dark background #0C0C14. CRITICAL LAYOUT: uniform 64x64 cells, no extra frames, no gaps, no scattered placement. Hard pixel edges, no anti-aliasing, no blur, zero alpha bleed.

Effect: Enemy death dissolve — red-black ash crumble (downward collapse). Use a generic enemy “unit silhouette” as the source shape (humanoid/monster-like but simple), centered and consistent scale across frames.

Frame beats (left→right):

1) Frame 1 (Flash): silhouette intact with a dark red flash pulse (deep crimson highlight clusters on edges + chest/core), then immediately starts to “fracture” (a few 1–2 px cracks/gaps). Keep flash controlled (no full-frame red).

2) Frame 2 (Start crumble): upper torso and head begin breaking into chunky red-black ash pixels; fragments fall 2–4 px downward; a few embers pop outward 1–2 px.

3) Frame 3 (Mid crumble): 50–70% collapsed; most mass now in mid-lower area; falling ash stream thicker; keep ash as discrete 1–3 px clusters (readable, not noisy).

4) Frame 4 (Last collapse): 85–95% gone; only a few lower fragments remain; ash gathers near the bottom as a small pile; minimal ember specks.

5) Frame 5 (End): small ash pile at the bottom edge (centered) with 1–2 fading ember pixels, then “empty” (either fully empty or near-empty with a couple dark specks max; prefer almost empty).

Palette/lighting:

- Ash: near-black + charcoal + dark maroon
- Embers: deep red-orange as tiny 1px accents only (very sparse)
- No glow bloom; any “heat” should be pixel-stepped and tight (1–2 px max)

Negative prompts: no smoke, no fog, no smooth gradients, no particles drifting upward, no other colors (no blue/green), no gore, no text, no watermark, no background scenery.')
ON CONFLICT (asset_key) DO UPDATE SET
  category = EXCLUDED.category, tier = EXCLUDED.tier, unity_path = EXCLUDED.unity_path,
  target_w = EXCLUDED.target_w, target_h = EXCLUDED.target_h, frame_count = EXCLUDED.frame_count,
  ppu = EXCLUDED.ppu, filter_mode = EXCLUDED.filter_mode,
  primary_color = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.primary_color, public.sprite_assets.primary_color),
  prompt_template = EXCLUDED.prompt_template;

INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('vfx_death_player', 'vfx', 'vfx', 'Sprites/VFX/vfx_death_player', 320, 64, 5, 32, 'Point', '#4488FF', 'Pixel art VFX sprite sheet, 5-frame horizontal strip, 320x64 total, exactly 5 frames in ONE ROW left-to-right, each frame 64x64. Dark background #0C0C14. CRITICAL LAYOUT: uniform 64x64 cells, no extra frames, no gaps, no scattered placement. Hard pixel edges, 1px dark outline only where needed, no anti-aliasing, no blur, zero alpha bleed.

Effect: Player unit death dissolve — blue-white particle disintegration (clean, readable at 1x). Use a simple humanoid “unit silhouette” as the source shape (generic, not class-specific), centered and consistent scale across frames.

Frame beats (left→right):

1) Frame 1 (Impact): full unit silhouette present, bright blue-white edge “overcharge” (1–2 px rim), brightest intensity; a few tiny motes start lifting from shoulders/head.

2) Frame 2 (Start dissolve): silhouette breaks into chunky pixel clusters from top-down; 15–25% of upper body becomes drifting particles. Motes move upward 2–4 px.

3) Frame 3 (Mid dissolve): 50–65% dissolved; remaining torso/legs fragmenting; particle column thicker above the head; keep particles as discrete 1–3 px clusters (no noise).

4) Frame 4 (Last fragments): 85–95% dissolved; only a few lower-body fragments remain; most particles now above where the head was (upward drift).

5) Frame 5 (Empty): no silhouette; only 0–2 faint lingering motes allowed, or completely empty (prefer empty if you want a clean end frame).

Palette/lighting:

- Core particles: icy white + pale cyan + mid sky-blue; minimal deep blue shadows for contrast
- Glow must be pixel-stepped (2–3 bands), no soft bloom
- Keep the brightest pixels limited (don’t fill the whole frame with white)

Negative prompts: no smoke, no fog, no smooth gradients, no lens flare, no sparks in other colors, no text, no watermark, no background scenery.')
ON CONFLICT (asset_key) DO UPDATE SET
  category = EXCLUDED.category, tier = EXCLUDED.tier, unity_path = EXCLUDED.unity_path,
  target_w = EXCLUDED.target_w, target_h = EXCLUDED.target_h, frame_count = EXCLUDED.frame_count,
