INSERT INTO public.sprite_assets (asset_key, category, tier, unity_path, target_w, target_h, frame_count, ppu, filter_mode, primary_color, prompt_template) VALUES ('vfx_status_liable', 'vfx', 'vfx', 'Sprites/VFX/vfx_status_liable', 192, 64, 3, 32, 'Point', '#7C4DFF', 'pixel art VFX sprite sheet, 3-frame looping strip, 192x64 total, each frame 64x64. Dark background #0C0C14. CRITICAL LAYOUT: exactly 3 frames in ONE ROW left-to-right, uniform 64x64 cells, no extra frames, no gaps, no scattered placement. Hard pixel edges, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no alpha bleed. No text, no watermark.

Effect: Liability chains overlay — thin void-violet chains wrapping around a unit silhouette (overlay VFX). Keep the chain shapes readable and not noisy: 2–3 chain loops max, crossing the center torso area with one loop lower (waist) and one loop upper (chest/shoulders). Palette: deep void violet + near-black shadows, with a tiny pale-violet highlight pixel on a few links only (no glow bloom).

3-frame “tighten pulse” cycle:

1) Frame 1: chains slightly loose (wider loops), links spaced a bit more, small slack curve on one side

2) Frame 2: chains tighten (loops shrink inward by 1–2 pixels), links look more compressed, add 1–2 pixel “strain” spark at one intersection

3) Frame 3: tightest state (loops smallest), intersection highlight shifts to a different link; then loop back to frame 1

Composition notes: leave the bottom 8–12 pixels relatively clear so it doesn’t conflict with feet/base VFX; keep chains centered and away from the frame edges.

Negative prompts: no metal shine gradients, no glowing runes, no lightning, no smoke/fog, no extra particles beyond 1–2 strain sparks.')
